      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes #62483.\n\nIn `DelegatingParser._apply_structural_tag` (`vllm/parser/abstract_parser.py`), when `--tool-strict-level` is not explicitly configured (`self.tool_strict_level is None`), `strict_level` unconditionally fell back to `tool_parser.default_tool_strict_level`.\n\nFor tool parsers whose `default_tool_strict_level` is `ToolStrictLevel.FUNCTION` (such as `Glm47MoeModelToolParser`, introduced in #56403), a request combining:\n- `tools` without `strict: true`,\n- `tool_choice=\"auto\"`, and\n- an explicit `response_format` (e.g., `json_schema` / `json_object`) or `structured_outputs`\n\nhad `strict_level` elevated to `ToolStrictLevel.FUNCTION`. As a result, `resolve_tool_strictness` treated the non-strict tools as active and `_apply_structural_tag` replaced `request.response_format` with `OrFormat(elements=[tools_structural_tag.format, output_format])`, allowing the model to emit `<tool_call>...` instead of adhering strictly to the caller's `response_format` schema (contrary to the `single_call` guard right below it: *\"Auto with structured outputs keeps its format-only grammar, so the flag never makes calls possible that are impossible without it\"*, and #56403's contract that requests with explicit structured outputs / JSON response format remain unchanged).\n\nThis PR guards the `tool_parser.default_tool_strict_level` fallback when `is_auto and structured_outputs is not None`, keeping `strict_level = ToolStrictLevel.AUTO` unless `--tool-strict-level` is explicitly configured by the operator or a tool has `strict: true`.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n```bash\npytest tests/parser/test_abstract_parser.py tests/tool_parsers/test_structural_tag_registry.py\n```\n\n## Test Result\n\n- `282 passed` across `tests/parser/test_abstract_parser.py` and `tests/tool_parsers/test_structural_tag_registry.py`.\n\n### Credits & Acknowledgments\n- Full credit to **@gringus** for reporting #62483, isolating the regression in `DelegatingParser._apply_structural_tag` where `tool_parser.default_tool_strict_level` (`ToolStrictLevel.FUNCTION`, introduced in #56403 by **@Dovis01**) overrides a caller's explicit `response_format` with `OrFormat` under `tool_choice=\"auto\"`, providing the minimal reproduction, and validating the fix.\n",
